# The console is served byte-for-byte over HTTP, and a test asserts that what the browser receives
# is exactly what is on disk (tests/test_web_bridge.py). With core.autocrlf=true and no rule here,
# git rewrites this file to CRLF on checkout while Python reads it back with universal newlines --
# so the bytes differ and the test fails on a fresh clone, on a colleague's machine and in CI,
# while passing on the machine where the file was last written. Pin it.
*.html text eol=lf

# Same reasoning for anything else read as bytes and compared, or fed to a parser that cares.
*.sql  text eol=lf
*.db   binary
*.wav  binary
